 a warning  some of the video is difficult to watch  it is still very early in the process  but researchers investigating possible  war crimes in bucha are already finding  evidence that points to something  horrible bodies that are being recovered  are having to have their hands unbound  we have a number of people  who  appear to have been killed with their  hands bound behind their backs using  plastic zip ties  at the local church no one knows exactly  how many bodies are in the fresh mass  graves there is however a count from one  day march 10th the priest says at least  68 bodies were collected from around  town on that day  and buried  here he says people were killed trying  to leave and their bodies were in the  streets they couldn't take them to the  cemetery going there was too dangerous  the town's mayor says any war is a crime  but they're still supposed to be rules  the way his citizens were treated was  something else  soldiers were deliberately killing  civilians and that the only way he can  describe it is genocide  that same word was used by ukraine's  president monday as he visited bucha  vladimir zolensky says walking the  streets understanding what happened  makes negotiating with the russian side  tougher  zalenski says they're finding bodies in  barrels and basements tortured and  executed war crimes one after another  there are unimaginable scenes in just  about every direction bodies on highways  in this case a family buried together at  least partially according to locals it  was the head of the village with her son  and husband they would have been killed  by russian soldiers who believe they  were helping ukrainian  troops investigators have a great deal  of work ahead of them  mike armstrong global news  and that is global national for this  monday i'm donna friesen we leave you  tonight with some sound and reflection  from a ukrainian musician  [Music]  his name is mark demianchenko he took  his guitar to the rubble of harkeev  where he lives one of the many once  vibrant places in ukraine now reduced to  a shadow of what it once was  we wish peace to everyone the 20 year  old says because without peace life is  very difficult  thanks for watching hope to see you here  again tomorrow  [Music]  [Music]  you
 

